#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pr-chain: review -> (fail) -> fix -> re-review loop for one PR at a time. A fresh agent runs every stage.

Usage:
  pr-chain pick [--all]                      table of open PRs and who owns them; the first eligible row is the next target
  pr-chain run <pr> [options]                run the loop on one PR
  pr-chain auto [options]                    first eligible PR; none -> first free issue (build, open DRAFT PR, run it); none -> scout files issues
  pr-chain issue <n> [options]               build one issue into a DRAFT PR, then run the loop on it
  pr-chain scout [options]                   a scout agent files new bug issues (status/ready-for-agent) and exits
  pr-chain resume [options]                  PRs waiting on a person: label human-approved -> CI + merge; comment -> fixer, loop restarts
  pr-chain land <pr> [options]               skip review/fix: gate + land the PR at its current head
  pr-chain models                            effective model per role (review/fix/gate/ui/build/scout) and its source
  pr-chain status                            one line per PR the chain has touched
  pr-chain report [--json] [--since DAYS] [--no-git] [--main BRANCH]
                                             read-only effectiveness report: end states, review rounds, minutes, rests, reverts (chain/report.py)
  pr-chain stop                              ask a running chain to stop after its current stage
  pr-chain clean <pr>                        remove the PR's leftover worktrees (never --force)

Options for run/auto/land:
  --max-rounds N      review/fix rounds before giving up (default 4)
  --review-model M    haiku (default) | sonnet | opus | codex[:slug]
  --fix-model M       haiku (default) | codex:gpt-6-luna | ...
  --gate-model M      final AUDITOR of the review stage's work, default opus; runs only after the reviewer says PASS; --no-gate skips it
  --max-audits N      audits per PR before NEEDS-HUMAN (default 2)
  --land              after PASS + gate + green CI, approve (non-author account) and merge. Without it the chain stops at READY.
  --ui-model M        vision model for UI PRs (default opus): runs ui-slop-review on real screenshots, assumes the UI is wrong
  --max-ui N          UI review failures before UI-FAILED (default 3); a FAIL goes to a fixer and only the UI review reruns
  --no-human          skip the human screenshot gate (post-UI-review PASS goes straight to CI/land)
  --vision-ok         a person already reviewed this head: skip the vision review and the human gate
  --build-model/--scout-model M, --scout-max N   builder for issues / scout and its issue cap
  --no-post           do not post verdict comments on the PR
  Model defaults: flag > env PR_CHAIN_<ROLE>_MODEL > <repo>/chain/models.json
    ({"review": "codex:gpt-6-luna", "fix": "codex:gpt-6.1-terra", ...}) > built-in. See `pr-chain models`.
  --dry-run           print what would happen, launch nothing, write nothing remote

Stages (each one a NEW agent): fold main in (no model) -> REVIEW-FIX (judge the exact head; after FAIL, fix in its worktree)
-> a fresh REVIEW-FIX ... -> PASS: GATE (read-only, non-Haiku) -> CI wait -> LAND.
Guards: one chain at a time, one claim per PR, STOP file, the settings-file damage tripwire after every agent (when
[tripwire] settings_file is set), per-agent tool-call budgets and agent timeout from flow.json (-1 = no limit),
no force push, never gpt-6-astra, repeated identical findings stop the loop (NEEDS-HUMAN).
Work, ledger and logs: the [paths] work folder (ledger.jsonl, prs/<n>/r<k>-<role>/). Uses the vendored agent-kit
(kit.py, land/fold.py, land/land_pr.py). Every project-specific value lives in pr-chain.toml (see chain/config.py).
"""
